        "sys_dao_marks"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Ming Tang valley is among the best places in Central Continent to produce light path Gu worms. That land of treasures is rich in light path dao marks, and almost every twenty years a wild light path Immortal Gu forms there.",
      "chapters": [
        1030
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "marks-that-birth-light-path-gu",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_ming_tang_valley",
        "reg_central_continent",
        "sys_gu_worms"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan’s immortal aperture has about a hundred or so light path dao marks, so it has some light and is not dim like his immortal zombie body’s dead aperture, yet that light is not enough for multicolored overlord flowers. The most basic solution is to increase the number of light path dao marks in the immortal aperture; light path Gu Immortals with deep foundation often have limitless illumination in theirs.",
      "chapters": [
        1083
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "illuminating-the-aperture",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_gu_immortal"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Tong Hua names a green desolate fungus on deep-sea corals light shine fungus. It contains light path dao marks and can emit strong light.",
      "chapters": [
        1296
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "light-shine-fungus",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_tong_hua"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Desolate plants as a tier are covered on desolate plant.",
      "chapters": [],
